The class `CompletableToObservable` is a thin delegating wrapper that merely forwards subscription from a `CompletableSource` to an `Observer`. Its behavior is trivial and its performance is dominated by the underlying `CompletableSource` implementation rather than the wrapper itself. Benchmarking this single method would not provide meaningful insight, and any micro‑benchmark would be heavily influenced by external factors (scheduler, upstream source, RxJava overhead). Therefore, a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.